### Syntax and Formatting

#### Switch Statement Indentation

```swift
// Good: Case statements indented one tab from switch
switch fileExtension {
	case "gpx":
		return try await parseGPX(data: data, fileName: fileName, userId: userId)
	case "tcx":
		return try await parseTCX(data: data, fileName: fileName, userId: userId)
	case "fit":
		return try await parseFIT(data: data, fileName: fileName, userId: userId)
	default:
		throw ActivityServiceError.unsupportedFileFormat(fileExtension)
}

// Bad: Case statements not indented
switch fileExtension {
case "gpx":  // Avoid - should be indented
	return try await parseGPX(...)
}
```

- Case statements inside switch statements must be indented one tab from the `switch` keyword
- This applies to all switch statements regardless of context

